WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.922
Errol Morris: You asked me about
the nature of our relationship.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.049
John le Carré: I needed to know
who I was talking to.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:10.552
Were you my friend across the fire?
Who are you?

00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:14.890
Errol Morris: And if I can't answer
that question?

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:18.852
♪

00:00:19.478 --> 00:00:22.356
John le Carré: It's terribly difficult
to recruit for a secret service.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.650
You're looking for somebody
who's a bit bad,

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.151
but at the same time, loyal.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:27.277
There's a type.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:29.780
And I fit it perfectly.

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:33.867
♪

00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:34.910
Errol Morris: In your memoir you say,

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.788
"None of it's true.
It's as I imagined it."

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.252
John le Carré: When I was in MI-6,
it wasn't enough for me.

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:45.921
So, what I did was
reinvent the secret world,

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:47.589
and fill my own people with it.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:53.637
♪

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.640
Errol Morris: Why is betrayal
an important concept to you?

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.809
John le Carré:
It has a long family background.

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.354
Writing is a journey of self-discovery.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:07.317
I see my own life as a succession
of embraces and escapes.

00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:10.571
(Music intensifies)

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:11.738
(Gunshot)

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:13.574
Errol Morris:
Maybe this is an interrogation.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.909
Maybe I am self-deceived.

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:17.077
I don't know.

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:20.706
But I'll answer any question
you wish me to answer,

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:22.291
as truthfully as I can.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.503
♪

